window.WIKI_ENTRY={"id": "concept-056", "name_zh": "价值完成", "name_en": "Value Fulfillment", "tagline": "赛斯说：宇宙不是要你“生存”就好，而是要你“完成”——每个意识单位天生带着一股把自身潜力推到最大、同时让整体也更好的驱策力，这就是价值完成。", "explanation": "价值完成（value fulfillment）是赛斯宇宙里最核心的法则之一：如果“成长”是物质宇宙最不可或缺的法则，那么“价值完成”就是在内在实相宇宙里与之对应的那条。它不是一个道德要求，而是刻在每个意识单位里的一股驱策力——把自身潜力推到最大，同时让整体也更好；它的个别完成，也增益其他每一个单位的更好发展。万物都为了整个建构的最佳完成而行动：原子有冲动，蜘蛛与苍蝇是共同参与者，每个族类都沉浸在自己的价值完成系统里。落到个人，你生来就在追求能增加生命品质的价值，在成就独属自己的存在时也丰富了世界；价值完成永远暗示对卓越（不是完美）的追求。自由意志不是它的障碍，反而是它被“内建”的方式——人格必须在被投射的层次上取得经验。它跟时间空间几乎无关，是一种“不占空间的扩展”；在梦里、在动物按强度的感知里最易体会。它也不是道德判罚：恶只是价值完成的付之阙如，爱才是已实现的价值完成，而它本身带着明显的快乐效应。把困难当冒险、追随快乐，就是顺着自己的价值完成去活。", "definitions": [{"zh": "如果成长是你们伪装宇宙中最不可或缺的法则之一，那么价值完成在内在实相宇宙里就是与之相应的东西。", "en": "If growth is one of the most necessary laws of your camouflage universe, value fulfillment corresponds to it in the inner reality universe.", "source": "Session 44"}, {"zh": "价值完成是存在于每个意识单位之内的一种心理上与物质上的倾向，把它以这样一种方式向着更大的完成推动，以至于它的个别完成也增益了每一个其他这种意识单位的可能最好发展。", "en": "Value fulfillment is a psychological and physical propensity that exists in each unit of consciousness, propelling it toward its own greatest fulfillment in such a way that its individual fulfillment also adds to the best possible development on the part of each other such unit of consciousness.", "source": "Session 868"}, {"zh": "每个人追求价值完成，而那是指他们以这样一种方式选择种种人生，使得他们所有的能力及才华可被尽可能的发展，并且以这样一种方式使得他们的世界也被丰富了。", "en": "Each person seeks value fulfillment, and that means that they choose various lives in such a fashion that all of their abilities and capacities can be best developed, and in such a way that their world is also enriched.", "source": "Session 911"}, {"zh": "价值完成永远暗示了对卓越的追求——不是完美，而是卓越。", "en": "Value fulfillment always implies the search for excellence—not perfection, but excellence.", "source": "Session 912"}], "blocks": [{"id": "B01", "title": "价值完成是什么：内在宇宙的“成长法则”", "note": "价值完成是赛斯宇宙里最核心的“法则”之一。他给了一个最简单的关系：如果“成长”是你们这个物质（伪装）宇宙最不可或缺的法则，那么“价值完成”就是在内在实相宇宙里与之对应的那条法则。这两条——价值完成与能量转换——都存在于“广阔的现在”里，加起来就成了“耐久性”（一种同时自发、同时发生的持久）。它不是一个道德要求，而是一种存在本身的倾向：心灵层面的成就，就是你们所知的价值完成；你这个“自己”会像细胞增殖那样，以价值完成的方式“进化”。所以别把它想成“变好”这种俗气说法，它是存在最重要的特性之一——万物都为了整个建构的最佳完成而行动。", "src": "第44、744、59、637、300、4、51、55节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 44 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 744 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 59 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 637 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 300 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 4 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 51 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 55 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-056-e0002", "zh": "我知道，这点资料难以理解，我在把它用尽可能简单的术语讲给你们听。如果成长是你们伪装宇宙中最不可或缺的法则的话，那么，在内在实相宇宙中相对应的就是价值完成（value fulfillment）。", "en": "I realize that this material is difficult, and I am giving it to you in as simple terms as possible. If growth is one of the most necessary laws of your camouflage universe, value fulfillment corresponds to it in the inner reality universe.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第44节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "44", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0006", "zh": "在你们特定的伪装宇宙中，你们正在学习能量转换。就你们来说，你们正在学习转化内在能量，把它塑造成物质建构，透过为了这个目的而形成的特定外在感官，这个层面让你们有能力操纵它们。但到目前为止，在能力的运用上，你们受到严重的限制。一旦你们精通了价值完成与能量转化这两条法则，自然而然就会耐久。", "en": "Now, on your particular camouflage universe you are learning energy transformation. And in your case you are learning to transform inner energy by forming it into physical constructions that the plane enables you to manipulate by the formation of particular outer senses for this purpose. You are severely limited as yet in the use of your abilities. When the two laws of value fulfillment and energy transformation are mastered, then duration is a natural consequence.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第44节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "44", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0159", "zh": "我在以尽可能简单的说法给你们这资料。如果生长是你们伪装宇宙的一个最必要的法则的话，那么“价值完成”在内在实相宇宙里就是与之相应的东西。", "en": "I am giving it [this material] to you in as simple terms as possible. If growth is one of the most necessary laws of your camouflage universe, value fulfillment corresponds to it in the inner-reality universe.4", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第744节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "744", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0161", "zh": "内在宇宙的第二个定律是能量转换。这经常在发生。能量转换与价值完成两者都存在于广阔的现在之内，加起来成了一个耐久性（durability），那在同时是自发的……而且是同时性的。", "en": "The second law of the inner universe is energy transformation.6 This occurs constantly. Energy transformation and value fulfillment, both existing within the spacious present [or at once], add up to a durability that is at the same time spontaneous … and simultaneous.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第744节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "744", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0042", "zh": "当然，和它有关的不是肉体的成长，而是心灵的成就，那就是你们知道的价值完成。我们将称这个为品质-深度（quality-depth加连字符），可是它和空间无关。这是一种在价值完成方面带着扩展的保证而存在的品质。", "en": "It has to do with not physical growth, of course, but with psychic fulfillment, which is as you know value fulfillment. We will call this quality-depth （hyphen）, and yet it has nothing to do with space. This is a quality existing with assurance of expansion, in terms of value fulfillment.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第59节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "59", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0155", "zh": "亲爱的读者，你是在扩展心灵结构的过程里，是在变成灵魂的一个有意识参与者的过程里，以某种方式来说，是在变成你的灵魂的过程里，就如细胞增殖、生长——在它们自己的天性和肉体架构之内——“自己”也是以价值完成④（value fulfillment）的方式在“进化”。", "en": "You, dear reader, are in the process of expanding your psychic structure, [of] becoming a conscious participator with the soul, in certain terms, [of] becoming what your soul is. As cells multiply and grow — within their own nature and the physical framework — so do selves “evolve” in terms of value fulfillment.*", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第637节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "637", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0117", "zh": "它们只是看起来不一样而已。在大多数情况下，自我觉察不到它离开一个物质有机体，在另一个里面成长。这是一次投射。我跟你说过，成长的年岁是幻相。价值完成是宇宙的法则，它在里面的系统之内看起来像是成长。", "en": "They simply appear to be different. As a rule the ego is not aware of its departure from one physical organism and its growth into another. This is a projection. The years of growth, as I have told you, are illusion. Value fulfillment is the law of the universe, and it appears as growth within your system.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第300节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "300", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0236", "zh": "以你们的说法，这意味着你并不需要单单只依赖你所认为的你的个人资源。基本上，价值完成是存在的最重要特性之一，因此，所有的东西都以提供整个建构整体的价值完成的最好方式个别地并一同地行动。", "en": "In your terms this means that you do not have to rely upon what you think of as your private resources alone. Basically (underlined), value fulfillment is one of the most important characteristics of existence, so that all things act individually and together in ways that best provide for the overall fulfillment of the entire construct.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第5节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "5", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0014", "zh": "从合作中，它们在某些方面实现一个价值完成。我说过，无限变动与蜕变的能力是内在宇宙的基本法则之一。这条法则反映在接近无限多样的结构，以及你们宇宙原子、分子与更小粒子所能达成的无限组合之中。", "en": "From their cooperation they achieve a value fulfillment along certain lines. I mentioned the capacity for infinite mobility and transmutation as being one of the laws of the inner universe. The reflection of this law is seen in the latent ability for almost infinite varieties of structures, and endless combinations that can be achieved by the atoms and molecules, and smaller particles of your universe.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第51节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "51", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0026", "zh": "他们恐惧自己会被消灭。我们正在思索的这种发展牵涉的却是一种扩展或延伸；同样的，扩展中的宇宙不占据空间，而是在价值完成方面扩展，所以扩展中的意识也不占据空间，但也是在价值完成方面扩展。这是你们的新大陆、你们的新挑战。", "en": "Many cavemen doubtlessly feared for their personal survival when they ventured forth upon the earth in daylight. They feared that their selves would be annihilated. Such a development as we are considering involves instead an expansion or extension; in the same manner that the expanding universe takes up no space, but expands in terms of value fulfillment, so the expanding consciousness would take up no space, but would also expand in terms of value fulfillment. This is your new frontier, your new challenge.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第55节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "55", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B02", "title": "它不在大小：刻在每一个意识单位里", "note": "这股驱策力不在大小、不在数目，而在每一个意识单位里。原子、质子都有朝向成长与价值完成的冲动；每只蜘蛛、每只苍蝇都带着“在生命中心”的内在推动力进入存在，而它们不是猎者与猎物，是更深过程里的共同参与者，一起朝某种“共同的价值完成”努力。每个族类都沉浸在自己的内在价值完成系统里，不只关心存活和繁殖，更关心它特有品质的强化与实现。所有已知物种在可见宇宙整体受孕时，就与生俱有地“在场”了。换句话说，价值完成是刻在每个意识单位里的心理与物质倾向——它的个别完成，也增益了其他每一个单位的更好发展。", "src": "第142、797、863、866、868、136、857节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 142 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 797 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 863 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 866 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 868 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 136 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 857 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-056-e0086", "zh": "再次地，没有理由因为个体是万众之一，就觉得他什么都不是。行动依据价值完成而发展，价值完成和尺寸或数目几乎没有关系；而且行动会转向意识。对它自己作用的行动变成意识，而说到意识，我的意思不一定是你们用这个词的意思。", "en": "Again, this is no reason to feel that the individual is nothing, simply because he is one of so many. Action develops according to value fulfillment, and value fulfillment has little to do with size or numbers; and action turns to consciousness. Action working on itself becomes consciousness, and in speaking of consciousness I do not necessarily mean what you mean by the word.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第142节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "142", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0170", "zh": "事实上，它们密切地觉知所有这种可能的合作的冒险，并生而具有价值完成（value fulfillment）的“动因”（drive）。那么，每个已知的物种是在可见宇宙的全盘孕育时，与生俱有地“在场”的。", "en": "They are innately aware, in fact, of all such probable cooperative ventures, and imbued with the “drive” for value fulfillment. Every known species was inherently “present” with the overall impregnation of the visible universe, then.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第797节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "797", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0177", "zh": "每个生灵体验到生命仿佛就在生命的中心。这适用于橱子里的一只蜘蛛，就像适用于任何的男人或女人一样。这个原则也同样适用于每个原子。意识的每个显现进入存在，感觉它安全的在生命之中心——透过它自己体验生命，透过它自己的本质觉察生命。它带着一种朝向价值完成的内在推动力进入存在。它在自己的环境里生就有一种安全感，而那个环境是适合它去处理的。它被给予朝向成长与行动的推动力，并且充满了去影响其世界之欲望。", "en": "Each being experiences life as if it were at life’s center. This applies to a spider in a closet as well as to any man or woman. This principle applies to each atom as well. Each manifestation of consciousness comes into being feeling secure at life’s center — experiencing life through itself,1 aware of life through its own nature. It comes into being with an inner impetus toward value fulfillment. It is equipped with a feeling of safety, of security within its own environment with which it is fit to deal. It is given the impetus toward growth and action, and filled with the desire to impress its world.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第863节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "863", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0179", "zh": "你们在和你们自己不同类的意识打交道，此其一。的确，它们是集中焦点的意识，每一个感觉它自己在生命的中心。不过，虽然如此，这些其他形式的意识也与它们由其中浮出的大自然之源头认同。以一种不可能解释的方式，那苍蝇与那蜘蛛是相连的，并且觉察到那联系。并不是作为猎者与猎物。却是作为在更深的过程里的个别参与者。它们一同努力朝向一种共同的价值完成，在其中，两个都获得了完成。", "en": "For one thing, you are dealing with different kinds of consciousness than your own. They are focused consciousnesses, surely, each one feeling itself at life’s center. While this is the case, however, these other forms of consciousness also identify then with the source of nature from which they emerge. In a way impossible to explain, the fly and the spider are connected, and aware of the connection. Not as hunter and prey, but as individual participants in deeper processes. Together they work toward a joint kind of value fulfillment, in which both are fulfilled.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第863节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "863", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0180", "zh": "每一种族类都被赋予了情绪上的感受，都沉浸在一种内在的价值完成系统里。那么，再次的，每一种族类不仅关怀肉体的幸存以及其成员的增值，并且也关怀它所特具的那些特定品质之加强与实现。", "en": "Each species is endowed with emotional feelings, immersed in an interior system of value fulfillment. Each species, again, then, is not only concerned with physical survival and the multiplication of its members, but [with] an intensification and fulfillment of those particular qualities that are characteristic of it.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第866节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "866", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0184", "zh": "你个人实质的存在，是因为生物性的存在于你们族类与所有其他族类之间的无与伦比的合作，而在较深的层面，则因为存在于所有族类的细胞之间的细胞性联盟。价值完成是存在于每个意识单位之内的心理上与物质上的倾向，把它以这样一种方式向着更大的完成推动，以至于它的个别完成也增益了每一个其他这种意识单位的可能最好发展。这种倾向在物质的架构之下与之内运作。它也在其之上运作，但我在这儿讲的是，价值完成赋予你们物质世界之内所有意识单位的合作性本质。", "en": "Individually, you exist physically because of the unsurpassed cooperation that exists just biologically between your species and all others, and on deeper levels because of the cellular affiliations that exist among the cells of all species. Value fulfillment is a psychological and physical propensity that exists in each unit of consciousness, propelling it toward its own greatest fulfillment in such a way that its individual fulfillment also adds to the best possible development on the part of each other such unit of consciousness. (Also see Session 863 at 9:21.) This propensity operates below and within the framework of matter. It operates above as well, but I am here concerned with the cooperative nature with which value fulfillment endows all units of consciousness within your physical world.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第868节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "868", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0084", "zh": "只是改变就允许本体在任何宇宙之内成为可能，因为没有改变，就没有价值完成、没有经验，也没有本体。电子宇宙的各部分被投射到很多场域。因此在很多场域之内，电某种程度被认为是一个实相。", "en": "Change alone allows for the possibility of identity within any universe, for without change there can be no value fulfillment, no experience, and no identity. Portions of the electrical universe are projected into many fields. Therefore electricity to some degree is recognized as a reality within many fields.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第136节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "136", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0172", "zh": "我为了一般大众的了解而用“冲动”这个名词，而以那种说法，分子与质子都有冲动。没有“意识”只是简单的对刺激反应，却都有它自己朝向成长与价值完成之冲动。对你们许多人而言，仿佛冲动是不可预测的、矛盾的、没有道理的、身体化学物反复无常的混合之结果，而你就会觉得它们必须被压碎，而怀着与以杀虫剂去喷蚊子同样致命的意图去消灭它。", "en": "(Pause at 10:04.) I am using the term “impulses” for the understanding of the general public, and in those terms molecules and protons have impulses. No consciousness simply reacts to stimuli, but has its own impulse toward growth and value fulfillment. It seems to many of you that impulses are unpredictable, contradictory, without reason, the result of erratic mixtures of body chemicals, and that they must be squashed with as much deadly intent as some of you might when you spray a mosquito with insecticide.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第857节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "857", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B03", "title": "你这辈子在追什么：个人层面的价值完成", "note": "落到你个人身上：每个人之内都有一股成长与价值完成的力量，那正是让肉体成长、让胎儿成形的力量。你生下来就在追求能增加生命品质的价值，在成就一个独属于你的存在状态的同时，也丰富了这世界。每个人追求的，是选那样一种人生——让所有的能力与才华尽可能发展，同时让世界也被丰富；有些人甚至故意选“缺陷”的身体，好更强烈地贯注于其他领域。价值完成永远暗示对“卓越”的追求——不是完美，而是卓越；它在任何领域的出现，都是一种灵性与生物指令的回音。连那个可怜、不快乐的有罪的自己，也是个在寻求自己救赎的心理结构，因为它也早已超过了定义它的旧框架。", "src": "第801、862、911、912、931、914、406、409节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 801 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 862 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 911 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 912 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 931 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 914 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 406 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 409 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-056-e0171", "zh": "（“每个人之内都有一种成长与价值完成（value fulfillment）的力量，那就是使得肉体的成长成为可能的力量，在胎儿背后的力量。在你事先就知道你将诞生其中的那个时期的本质，你俩都生而具有某种能力，而你们事先就知道了。如果你们要让这些能力有用到的机会，你们就必须扩大传统观念的架构。就某种意义而言，它们给了你俩第二个生命，因为在旧的架构里没有一条可以令你们满足或是具有创造性的路子可走。”", "en": "(“There is a power of growth and value fulfillment within each individual that must be satisfied. It is the power that makes physical growth possible, the power that is behind the fetus. You know ahead of time the nature of the period into which you will be born. You [Jane and Rob, or Ruburt and Joseph] were both born with certain abilities, and you knew ahead of time that you would have to enlarge the framework of conventional concepts if you were to have room to use those abilities. In a way, they gave you both a second life, for in the old framework there was no satisfying [underlined] or creative way to go. (“You have both used the material I have given you, and what you have learned on your own through the material, very well — some of it so smoothly that you are not even aware of your accomplishments. In some areas you still cling to old beliefs, but there is no end to what you can do, still, with growing comprehension. That is, you can still accomplish as much, if not more, than you already have.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第801节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "801", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0174", "zh": "你生下来就有爱心，你生下来就有慈悲心，你生下来就对你自己及你的世界好奇。那些属性也属于自然律。你生下来就知道你拥有一个独特而切身的存在感，而它寻求自己的圆满以及其他人的圆满。你生下来就在追求理想的实现。你生下来就在追求能增加生命品质的价值，把特性、能量与能力加在生命上，那是只有你能个人的贡献给世界的。你生下来就在追求达到一种你独特的存在状态，同时也丰富了这世界的价值完成。", "en": "You are born loving. You are born compassionate. You are born curious about yourself and your world. Those attributes also belong to natural law. You are born knowing that you possess a unique, intimate sense of being that is itself, and that seeks its own fulfillment, and the fulfillment of others. You are born seeking the actualization of the ideal. You are born seeking to add value to the quality of life, to add characteristics, energies, abilities to life that only you can individually contribute to the world, and to attain a state of being that is uniquely yours, while adding to the value fulfillment of the world.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第862节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "862", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0203", "zh": "每个人追求价值完成，而那是指他们以这样一种方式选择种种人生，使他们所有的能力及才能可以尽可能的发展，并且以这样一种方式使他们的世界也被丰富了。有些人会故意选择“缺陷的”身体，以便更强烈的贯注于其他领域。他们想要一种不同的焦点。（停顿良久。）他们想以某种模式过滤他们的特性。这样的选择要求一种强化，那种强化使加诸个人方面及双亲方面的，因此，某一群人会以一种极为特征性的方式与世界产生联系。在几乎所有这种例子里（停顿），这种人也会从事于否则可能不会被考虑的主观议题或问题，他们会问就他们自己而言必须提出的问题，不只为他们自己，也为整个的社会。", "en": "Each person seeks value fulfillment, and that means that they choose various lives in such a fashion that all of their abilities and capacities can be best developed, and in such a way that their world is also enriched. Some people will choose “defective” bodies purposely in order to focus more intensely in other areas. They want a different kind of focus. (Long pause.) They want to sift their characteristics through a certain cast. Such a choice demands an intensification. It is made on the part of the individual and on the parts of the parents as well, so that a certain group of people will relate to the world in a highly characteristic way. In almost all such cases (pause), such people will be embarked upon subjective issues and questions also that might not be considered otherwise. They will ask questions on their own parts that need to be raised, not only for themselves but for the society at large.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第911节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "911", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0205", "zh": "价值完成永远暗示了对卓越的追求——不是完美，而是卓越。在任何既定领域——情感上、身体上、理性上、直觉上、科学上——的卓越是反映在其他领域的，而其存在本身就有作为一个成就的楷模的作用。那么，这种卓越并不需要被结够到生命的任何一面里，虽然它可能出现在任何一面里。而不论它在何处出现，它都可说是一个灵性上及生物上的指令的回音。以你们的说法，有不同历史时期的人类曾显示出他们能做什么，以及在某些特定的方向什么是可能的，当基因性与转世性的扳机被触动，并且完全打开，以致某些特征以其最清楚、最壮观的方式出现，以作为一个个别的示范以及给整个人类的示范。", "en": "Value fulfillment always implies the search for excellence—not perfection, but excellence. Excellence (pause) in any given area—emotional, physical, intellectual, intuitional, scientific—is reflected in other areas, and by its mere existence serves as a model for achievement. This kind of excellence need not be structured, then, into any one aspect of life, though it may appear in any aspect, and wherever it appears it is an echo of a spiritual and biological directive, so to speak. There are different historical periods, in your terms, where the species has showed what it can do—and what is possible in certain specific directions when the genetic and reincarnational triggers are touched and opened full blast, so that certain characteristics appear in their clearest, most spectacular light, to serve as individual models and as models for the species as a whole.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第912节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "912", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0217", "zh": "（“他的诗在某方面有刺激的作用。也许带着一些夸大，但你也许可以说那突破是一个救命的东西，因为如果没有某些这种扩展，鲁柏会觉得无法继续他特定的那种存在。不可能以语言说出一个人或另一个人在人生中寻找什么，或哪些物质最能提升他的成长或发展，甚至同类的两株植物有时也要求完全不同的照顾。那么，这些课打开了对鲁柏的存在那很自然的特定一种价值完成之门。到某个程度，那可怜的、不快乐的有罪的自己，一个由信念与感受形成的心理结构，也在寻求自己的救赎，因为甚至它也已超过了那如此界定它的架构。”", "en": "“His poetry acted in some regards as a stimulator. That breakthrough, you might say, with perhaps some exaggeration, was a lifesaver, for without some such expansion Ruburt would have felt unable to continue the particular brand of his existence. It is not possible to say in words what one person or another looks for in life, or what unique features best promote his or her growth and development. Even two plants of the same kind sometimes require completely different treatments. The sessions, then, opened the door to a particular kind of value fulfillment that was natural to Ruburt’s being. Now to some extent it was that poor, unhappy sinful self, a psychological structure formed by beliefs and feelings, that was also seeking its own redemption, since even it had outgrown the framework that so defined it.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第931节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "931", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0208", "zh": "可是，人类真正的移动一直是心理性的，或如果你喜欢的话，是心灵性的，涉及了概念的探索。而再次的，以那种说法，人类的存活基本上是依赖它对其存在的有意义之信念。（强调的：）不过，这些新的宗教或团体，因而随着基因性的智慧之路，打开了臆测与信念的新领域。而如果它们目前的某些信念以理智的理由来看是很可笑的话——因为这种团体是跟随价值完成的指令，所以不论多微弱——那些信念终究是意味深长的。就你们习惯运用的理智而言，很容易只看到这种团体滑稽的行为，那样看来，它可以显得非常可笑。", "en": "The true motion of the species, however, has always been psychological, or psychic if you prefer, involving the exploration of ideas. And again, the survival of the species in those terms is basically dependent upon its belief in the meaningfulness of its existence. (Emphatically:) These new cults and groups, however—these new cults and groups, therefore—therefore—are following the paths of genetic wisdom, opening up new areas of speculation and belief. And if some of their present beliefs are ludicrous in the light of the intellect’s reason, in the end—because [such groups] are following the dictates of value fulfillment, however feebly—they are significant. It is easy for the intellect, as you are used to using it, to see only the antics of such groups, and they can appear ridiculous in that light.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第914节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "914", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0134", "zh": "从更宽广的角度来看，实相一词和我将提供给你们的那些特征，都将视为联合心灵意识的重要部分，所有其他意识都源自于这个心灵意识。这些新出现的意识形成了新的片刻点，也创造新的价值充盈经验，而这些经验又不断创造出整体实相，即使这个整体实相也仍在持续创造。", "en": "In larger terms, the word reality and those characteristics that I will give you as attributed to it, will be seen as part and parcel of a unified psychic consciousness, from which all other consciousness emerges. These emerging consciousness form new moment points, create new value fulfillment experiences that constantly allow the overall reality to be created even as it creates.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第406节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "406", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0136", "zh": "但是，由于种种原因，这种情况有些时间内不会出现。如果人们因为知道死亡并不存在而停止杀戮，那么就无法在某些重要方向上达成价值充盈。尽管他相信死亡确实存在，但他必须停止杀戮，他必须在发生问题的脉络中解决问题。", "en": "This will not come however for many reasons, for some time. Value fulfillment would not be achieved in some important directions if man ceased killing because he knew death did not exist. He must cease killing while he believes death does exist. He must solve the problem in the context that it developed.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第409节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "409", "only_en": true}]}]}, {"id": "B04", "title": "自由意志不是障碍：它内建了“必须去完成”", "note": "自由意志不是价值完成的障碍，反而是它被“内建”的方式。赛斯说，所谓自由意志唯一的弊端，就是内建的价值完成之必要性——人格必须在它被投射的特定层次上取得经验，别无选择；这股朝价值完成的强迫作用，是经验需求里自带的东西。当自我明白自己是整体行动的一部分，它就不会再怕自己的耐久性，因为它会了悟：身为行动的一部分，它的本性就建立在改变、活力与价值完成上。价值完成在这个区域“相当于你们的时间”；你知觉什么、就被什么改变，而知觉者与知觉根本是同一回事——这里，已经接近价值完成的真义了。", "src": "第95、161、429、462、269、151、398、426节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 95 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 161 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 429 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 462 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 269 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 151 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 398 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 426 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-056-e0068", "zh": "人格带着你可以称为的自我决定权（self-determination）和自由意志的配备，自己打天下。如果你从头到尾记得我们谈价值完成的资料，就会知道所谓自由意志唯一一个弊端就是内建的价值完成。换句话说，人格一定要在它运作的一个特定存在层次之上或之内得到经验，除此之外它别无选择。它一定要体验它已经被投射的特定层次上的存在。", "en": "The personality is on its own, with what you may call the power of self-determination and free will. If you had thoroughly remembered our material on value fulfillment, you would know that the only detriment to so-called free will is the built-in necessity for value fulfillment. The personality must gain experience, in other words, on a particular level of existence, on which or within which it operates, and it cannot choose otherwise. It must experience existence on the particular level on which it has been projected.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第95节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "95", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0070", "zh": "现在。没有其他内建的指令，也没有其他禁令。但是，当然这个经验需求的内建指令，就是朝向价值完成的强迫作用，而且你知道这不仅仅适用于成长而已，其实成长本身只是朝着一个方向的一种价值完成的物质化伪装而已。", "en": "Now. No other commands are built-in, no other prohibitions given. But built in of course into this necessity for experience, is the compulsion toward value fulfillment, and as you know this does not apply alone to growth, which is in itself a camouflage materialization of value fulfillment along one line only.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第95节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "95", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0104", "zh": "换句话说，自我表面上的激烈反应只是一个骗术而已，为的是要掩盖它拒绝涉入整体行动的事实，因为担心耐久性不保。一旦自我了解，而它也会了解，它是全我的一部分，也是行动的一部分，此时真的就不会担心自身的耐久性，因为它会了悟到，身为行动的一部分时，它的本性就建立在改变、活力与价值完成上面。", "en": "In other words the apparent intensity of the egotistical reactions is a sham on the part of the ego, to hide the fact that it refuses to become involved with action as a whole, because it fears for its permanence. When the ego understands, and it will, that it is a portion of the whole self, and itself a part of action, then indeed it will not fear for its own permanence, for it will realize that being a part of action, its very nature is dependent upon change, and vitality, and value fulfillment.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第161节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "161", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0143", "zh": "在那个区域里，价值完成就相当于你们的时间。你们可以休息一下，我们再继续。", "en": "Value fulfillment corresponds to your time in that area. You may take a break and we will continue.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第429节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "429", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0152", "zh": "现在我告诉你们：知觉者被他所知觉的东西改变了，而他同时也改变那被知觉的东西。知觉者与知觉，从根本上说就是同一回事。在这里，我们已经接近价值完成与片刻点的含义。", "en": "Now I tell you that while the perceiver is changed by what he perceives, he also changes that which is perceived. Perceiver and perception, in a basic manner, are one and the same. Here we come close to the meaning of value fulfillment and moment points.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第462节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "462", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0113", "zh": "人的一生寿命不过是一个片刻点而已。自我是你能够用来探索和体验这个片刻点的那个部分。(微笑）价值完成需要感知的这种减速。这很难解释。想想心理时间的运用。你在物理时间的几个物理时刻之内获得经验，这些经验完全独立于你们的时间结构之外。", "en": "The span of a whole man’s lifetime is no more than a moment point. The ego is the portion of you equipped to explore and experience this moment point in depth. （Smile.） Value fulfillment demands this slowing down of perception. This is most difficult to explain. Consider using psychological time. You have experiences within a few physical moments of physical time, experiences that are entirely independent of your time structure.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第269节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "269", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0097", "zh": "自我是自己体验时间连续性的那一部分，对它来说，经验是一连串的刺激和回应，一个接着一个继续下去。然而这本身，可以说就是一种区分，或是一种价值完成，因为任何行动的同时性本质在这里都是以慢动作被经验，就像小孩必须先学走才能跑一样。", "en": "The ego is that portion of the self which experiences time as continuity, and to whom experience is a series of stimuli and responses carried on one after another. And yet this is in itself a division, so to speak, or a kind of value fulfillment, for the simultaneous nature of a given action is here experienced in slow motion, as a child must learn to walk before the child can run.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0132", "zh": "我在这个房间里，但我也在另一个时间和另一个地方。你父亲同时可以在几个层面当中，所有这些都是价值充盈，这就是成长。 我们与鲁柏一起做得很好。事实上，我们这么清晰透了过来，所以他现在正在学习如何摆脱掉我的束缚。我愿意离开，但我的能量非常强大，导致他不知道该如何甩掉我。他完全放松，感觉到我的存在，而他还不会习惯。", "en": "Now, I am here in this room. I am also in another place in another time. Your father is in several dimensions at once. All of this is value fulfillment. It is growth. We are doing well with Ruburt. We are coming through so clearly in fact that he is now in the process of learning how to disentangle himself from me. I leave willingly, but my energy is so strong that he does not know how to let me go. He is fully relaxed. He is not used to feeling my presence however so strongly", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第398节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "398", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0140", "zh": "然而，有一个自己早已走过了这些路径，这些其他的自己只是他的一部分。这个自己在梦里以及解离的状态中，与这些所谓的“上升”的自己沟通。但随着这个自己在价值完成中的成长，他能够觉察到其他线上那些别的旅人——在他看来，他们似乎是未来的自己。", "en": "There is however a self who has already traveled these routes, of whom these other selves are but part. This self, in dreams and dissociated conditions, communicates with these various quote “ascending” selves. But as the self grows in value fulfillment, he can become aware of these other travelers on other threads, who might seem to him to be future selves.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第426节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "426", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B05", "title": "爱、恶与快乐：它不是道德判罚", "note": "价值完成不是道德判罚，别拿它当尺子量人。你们所谓的“恶”，只是在某个特定情况下价值完成的付之阙如；恐惧来自缺乏了解、缺乏价值完成，而恨就是“不是爱”的东西——爱，则是已实现或正在实现的价值完成。小孩不因为幼稚就是邪恶的，价值完成一直在起作用。它也带着明显的“快乐”效应：人或自然不是拼命去满足需求，而是活力洋溢地去追快乐，而在追快乐的过程里，需求也被满足了。连动物和植物都不只关心存活，还关心一种“情感品质”——追求对意识条件的完整欣赏与创造性延伸。可能性也依照价值完成而扩展，一件事会朝无限方向生出枝杈。", "src": "第145、397、304、933、935、413、71、438节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 145 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 397 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 304 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 933 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 935 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 413 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 71 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 438 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-056-e0088", "zh": "——你们所谓的恶代表着，在一个特定或任何一个特定的情况中，价值完成的付之阙如。我相信你知晓，一直都有那些招致不公不义和迫害的人，一直都有那些施行迫害的人。有那些谋杀的人，也有那些企图被杀害的人。", "en": "—that which you call evil represents a falling short of value fulfillment in a particular, or in any particular, case. There are always, as I believe you realize, those who court injustice and persecution. There are always those who persecute. There are those who murder, and there are those who seek to be slain.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第145节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "145", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0090", "zh": "恨是没有理智的恐惧。恐惧是缺乏了解、缺乏价值完成引起的。恨就是那不是爱的东西。爱是已实现的，或实现中的，价值完成。它就是行动，而且它认识它自己，它在它各个部分中发光发热，它分离以便认识它自己，而且因为认识它自己，所以不再分离。", "en": "Hate is unreasoning fear. Fear is caused by lack of understanding, by a lack of value fulfillment. Hate is that which is not love. Love is fulfilled, or fulfilling, value fulfillment. It is action that knows itself, and that glorifies in its parts, that is separated to know itself, and in knowing itself is no longer separated.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第145节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "145", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0131", "zh": "小孩并不邪恶，因为他不是大人，不能因为他的幼稚而受到审判。价值充盈一直在起作用，这两句话之间——你明白我指的是什么——仍然存在着审判的观念，就像是一种动力或鞭策，让内我对必将出现的成长有所认识。", "en": "The child is not evil because he is not a man, and cannot be judged for his childishness. Value fulfillment is always working, yet there is between those two statements—you realize the ones to which I refer—the idea of judgment as an impetus and spur against the inner self s knowledge of the growth that must come.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第397节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "397", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0119", "zh": "因此，在这个脉络之中，你们必须温柔对待活生生的东西。它们是你们系统之内的现实。在你们的层面上，一定要小心翼翼把建设性的情感注入哲学信条之中。在你所在之处，有极大的价值完成将会实现。知道你在哪里以及你的实相本质，这是好事。但是，你仍然必须在它的架构之内运作。", "en": "Therefore, within this context you trust treat your living things gently. They are actualities within your system. Philosophical tenets at your level must be carefully filled in by constructive Emotions. There is strong value fulfillment to be gained where you are. It is good to know where you are, and the nature of your reality. You must still operate within its framework, however.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第304节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "304", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0225", "zh": "心理学家常常谈到人的需求，反之，在此我想谈谈人的快乐（pleasure）。因为价值完成一个明显的特性，就是快乐的效应。人或自然并非那么想去满足需求，却是去活力洋溢的、放任的追求快乐——而透过追随快乐，每个有机体也找到并且满足需求。不过，在人生的体验里，所涉及的远超过起码需求的满足，因为生命处处都具有一个向往品质的欲望——一个承认快乐本身之肯定特质的品质。", "en": "Psychologists often speak of the needs of man. Here I would like to speak instead of the pleasures of man, for one of the distinguishing characteristics of value fulfillment is its pleasurable effect. It is not so much that man or nature seeks to satisfy needs, but to exuberantly, rambunctiously seek pleasure—and through following its pleasure each organism finds and satisfies its needs as well. Far more is involved in the experience of life, however, than the satisfaction of bare needs, for life is everywhere possessed with a desire toward quality—a quality that acknowledges the affirming characteristics of pleasure itself.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第933节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "933", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0228", "zh": "那些基因顺序如此平顺的追随价值完成的追求，以致任何时候当条件适合时，它们都可以被重新启动——因为即使动物也不只光是关怀幸存而已，植物亦然，却还关怀我只能称为（停顿良久）情感品质的东西。那些品质追求对那些意识的条件一个完全的欣赏及创造性的延伸，那些“意识的条件”既标示每个族类为它自己，也将它与所有其他族类联合在一起。", "en": "Those sequences follow the pursuits of value fulfillment so smoothly that they can be reactivated whenever the conditions are fortunate—for even the animals are not concerned with simple survival alone, nor the plants, but with what I can only call (long pause) emotional qualities: qualities that seek a full appreciation and creative extension of those conditions of consciousness that stamp each species as itself and yet join it with all others.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第935节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "935", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0138", "zh": "心理存在的前提是经验，一种在价值充盈（停顿）、情感操控和主观状态的直接理解等方面的经验。这涉及了一种本领和能力，能将自己全心全意投入一种被实相包围的情境，而且又能觉知到那个如此失落或被包围的自己。（停顿；强烈的语气）", "en": "A psychological existence presupposes experience, experience in terms of value fulfillment (pause) and the Emotional manipulation and direct knowledge of subjective states. This involves a capacity and ability to throw yourself wholeheartedly into a reality enveloping situation, and yet to be aware of the self who is then so lost or enveloped. (Pause; emphatic delivery.)", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第413节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "413", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0054", "zh": "再说一次，组成种子的物质绝对没有持续性，组成草的物质也一样没有。你们有的其实是在物质背后那个意识的价值完成，它以各种不同的形态扩展与展现它自己。", "en": "Again, there is absolutely no continuity in the matter that composes the seeds, and the matter that composes the grass. What you have instead is the value fulfillment of the consciousness behind matter, as it expands and expresses itself in various forms.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第71节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "71", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0148", "zh": "可能性依照价值完成而扩展。因此一个特定的作为并不必然导致作为B和作为C，进而导致一个收尾的行动。它反倒朝无限的方向生出枝杈，而那些枝杈又有枝杈。在这里，谈创造的两难的那些课，以及谈相对的非存在的那些课，会帮到你们。", "en": "Probabilities expand in terms of value fulfillment. One given act does not necessarily then lead to act B and C, and hence to a concluding action. Instead it has offshoots in infinite directions, and these offshoots have offshoots. Sessions on the creative dilemmas and the sessions dealing with relative nonbeing will help you here.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第438节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "438", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B06", "title": "死亡、梦与“不占空间的扩展”", "note": "价值完成跟你们熟悉的时间、空间几乎没关系。它不是占空间的扩展，而是在“不占空间的深度”方面扩展；梦宇宙最能帮你懂这个概念——在梦里没有物质结构，行动更自发流畅，因为价值完成被赋予了更大的支配权。记忆、经验与价值完成不会随着内在扬弃一个形式而丧失，那会否定价值完成本身。当意念不再需要物质具体化，时间概念就无用武之地，取而代之的是“经验的强度与价值完成”。动物、植物、石头都按强度感知，在品质与价值完成方面，它们有比你们更宽的“当下”。无限也和价值完成有关——它是“变为”的状态，永远不可能结束，因为它永远不会完成。", "src": "第108、115、149、430、433、305、95、96节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 108 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 115 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 149 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 430 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 433 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 305 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 95 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 96 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-056-e0076", "zh": "因此，这内在（inwardness）穿流并形成物质，当它完成任何既定形式的表达时，这内在就会留下来。你们知道就人来说，记忆、经验和价值完成并不会随着内在扬弃一个形式而丧失。这会否定价值完成本身。", "en": "The inwardness therefore flows through and forms matter, and the inwardness remains when it has finished expression in any given form. As you know in the case of man, memory, experience and value fulfillment is not lost as the inwardness disregards one form. This would deny value fulfillment itself.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第108节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "108", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0082", "zh": "梦宇宙也丰富你们自己的存在。可以这么说，这里有着极大的相互影响，和一种持续的能量交流，而且是透过它们不断经过场域之间而被转化和充电的能量。梦，也许比任何别的东西还要清楚，可以帮助你们了解价值完成，以及不占空间的扩展观念。", "en": "The dream universe also enriches your own existence. There is great interplay here, and a continual interchange of energies, and of energies that are transformed and recharged, so to speak, through their constant passage between fields. Dreams, perhaps more clearly than anything else, can help you understand the concept of value fulfillment, and of the expansion that does not take up space.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第115节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "115", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0092", "zh": "从连续性的角度来看，在梦宇宙里，时间显然不是一个重要元素，而这也是梦宇宙里没有物质结构的原因之一。这里直觉和某些内在能力的自由度高很多，所以不需要以任何禁锢的形式或结构使用分子。在梦宇宙之内，行动更自发、更流畅。意象的出现与消失也快很多，因为价值完成被赋予更大的支配权。", "en": "Obviously, time in terms of continuity, is not an element of importance in the dream universe, and this is one of the reasons for the lack of physical structure. The intuitions and certain inner abilities here have so much more freedom that it is unnecessary for molecules to be used in any imprisoning form or structure. Action is more spontaneous within the dream universe, more fluid. The images appear and disappear much more quickly because value fulfillment is allowed greater reign.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第149节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "149", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0095", "zh": "这个圆没有特定的边界，可以向外无限扩大。在梦宇宙里，在所有这种性质的系统里，发展不是借由在你们单一线条上的旅行来达成，而是透过你钻进你们所谓片刻的那个点来达成。在这样一个价值完成系统之内，物理定律完全不适用。基本上，你们自己的物质宇宙就在这种系统的切点上，而且，从我的观点来看，经验之所以出现得这么缓慢，纯粹是此一切点的目的和本质所致。此一切点，以某种方式，被你们这么缓慢地追逐，以致看起来像在一条连续线上间隔排列的一连串事件。你们体验的行动之所以是一个接着一个的事件，原因并不是出于行动本身的性质，而是你们自己的结构和感知的本质。", "en": "There is no particular boundary to the circle. It widens outward indefinitely. Now. In the dream universe, in all systems of such nature, development is achieved not by traveling your single line, but by delving into that point that you call a moment. The physical laws simply do not apply here, within such a value fulfillment system. Basically your own physical universe is at the apex of such a system itself, and it is only because of the purpose and nature of the particular apex that experience appears, from my viewpoint, to be so slowed down. The particular point, in one manner, is being pursued by you in such a slow fashion that it appears to be a series of happenings strung out in a thread of continuity. You experience action as one happening after another, not because of the nature of action itself but because of the nature of your own structure and perception.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第149节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "149", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0145", "zh": "当观念不再需要物质的具体化时，时间观念便毫无用处了。经验的强度与价值完成取代了时间的位置。用你们的话说，种种开展同时打开。内在事件的组织，是按照各个人格的内在兴趣、以及任一事件被体验的强度来管理的。", "en": "When idea no longer needs physical materiaizationl, then the time concept is useless. Intensity of experience and value fulfillment takes time's place. Developments open, in your terms, at once. Organization of inner events is managed according to the inner interests of the various personalities and the intensities with which any given event is experienced.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第430节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "430", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0147", "zh": "这并不等于说，它们还不够先进、理解不了你们时间的实相。它们并不共享这个幻觉。几乎所有的动物、植物、鸟类、昆虫、石头与树木，都是按照强度来感知的。（长停顿。）一次经验的强度就是它们的当下；但在许多我现在不会向你们解释的方面，它们的当下比你们的持续得更宽。这并不必然意味着，它们在当下里感知到的过去与未来比你们感知的更多，因为它们并不用那些（加下划线）术语。但就品质与价值完成而言，那里有更大的持续性，而那加了引号的“片刻”被感知得更强烈。", "en": "This does not mean that they are not advanced enough to understand the reality of your time. They do not share the illusion. Almost all animals, plants, birds, insects, rocks and trees perceive according to intensities. (Long pause.)The intensity of an experience is their present; but in many ways that I will not explain to you at this point, their present is of wider duration than yours. This does not necessarily mean that they perceive more of the past and future within their present than you do, for they do not in those (underlined) terms. But in terms of quality and value fulfillment there is greater duration and the “moment,” in quotes, is more intensely perceived.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第433节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "433", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0120", "zh": "无限与你所知的空间或时间一点关系都没有。无限是变为的状态，而且永远不可能结束，因为它永远不会完成。无限与价值完成，以及全新可能性的开展、片刻点的探索、穿越不断创造时间幻相的维度之旅有关系。但是，既然没有时间，有什么好结束的呢？", "en": "Infinity has nothing to do with space or time as you know it. Infinity is the state of becoming and can never have an end for it is never completed. Infinity has to do with value fulfillment, and the unfoldings of ever new possibilities, the exploration of moment points, the traveling through dimensions that ever creates the illusion of time. But since there is no time, what is there to end?", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第305节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "305", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0066", "zh": "菲利普应该读一读特别讲到宇宙法则，也就是宇宙的内在法则那几节，进而体会在所有的宇宙之内的这个宇宙既自发又耐久。重复那个冗长的讨论是开倒车，但是，就像内在宇宙有自发和耐久的属性，就像广阔的现在同时存在又涵盖所有的过去和所有的现在以及所有的未来，就像菲利普了解扩展的意义，不在于时间或空间，而在于价值完成，这样他就能凭直觉理解到，当我说宇宙没有开始也没有结束时，与现有的实相没有任何矛盾（contradiction）。（注：重新编译。）", "en": "Philip should read the sessions dealing particularly with the laws of the universe, that is with the inner laws of the universe, appreciating then the facts that this universe within all universes is spontaneous while having durability. It would be backtracking to repeat that long discussion, but as the inner universe has as its attributes spontaneity and durability, and as the spacious present is simultaneous while containing within it all pasts and all presents and all futures, and as Philip understands the meaning of expansion in terms not of time or of space but of value fulfillment, so will he intuitively then grasp that no contradiction occurs with actual reality when I say that there is no beginning and no end.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第95节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "95", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0072", "zh": "这种扩展来自于能量的一种收缩，但因为价值完成与广阔的现在固有的独特属性，根本没有最初或第一次的收缩或扩展。", "en": "The expansion resulted from a contraction of energy, but because of the unique attributes inherent in both value fulfillment and in the spacious present, there simply was not an initial or first contraction or expansion.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第96节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "96", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0093", "zh": "不过，在梦宇宙里，较为缓慢的物质成长过程被心灵和心智的价值完成取代，而没有必要把分子长期囚禁在模式之内。", "en": "In the dream universe however the slower physical growth process is replaced by psychic and mental value fulfillment, which does not necessitate any long-range imprisonment of molecules within a pattern.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第149节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "149", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B07", "title": "物种、合作与“治疗法”：放大到全体", "note": "放大到物种与全体：所有物种都被价值完成鼓动，每个都寻求为自己、也为其他所有族类增添生命的质量。这个特性恐怕是一切万有这存在中最重要的成分，也是所有物种传承的一部分。意识单位（CU）在伦理上代表了世界在价值完成中的壮观基础——每个单位彼此相关、互为对方的一部分。当一种生命形式被逼违背自己的价值完成，就涉及了生物上的侵犯；赛斯说，正是这种对待其他生命的态度，让二战集中营的恐怖成为可能。历经多世转世，心灵在价值完成方面的成长，惊人得不下于胎儿长成成人。连所谓的“小神”们，价值完成也比你们深得多；心理结构也透过价值完成不断扩大自己形成新实相的能力。", "src": "第881、884、889、910、446、306、305、152节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 881 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 884 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 889 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 910 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 446 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 306 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 305 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 152 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-056-e0189", "zh": "我希望让你们看，所有的物种都被我所谓的价值完成所鼓动，在其中每个寻求为它自己并同时为其所有其它族类增添生命的质量。", "en": "We begin again with a new book, and I am sure your own lively mind will bring questions to the forefront that will be of interest. A fond good evening.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第881节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "881", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0191", "zh": "再次的，实际上所有这一切即刻发生。然而，包含在其中的心理经验的深度是无法测量的，因为这涉及了一种价值完成，而每一个意识都涉入其中。那价值完成的特性，恐怕是一切万有这存在中最重要的成分，而且也是一切物种的传承的一部分。", "en": "Again, in actuality all of this took place at once, yet the depth of psychological experience contained therein can never be measured, for it involved a kind of value fulfillment with which each consciousness is involved. That characteristic of value fulfillment is perhaps the most important element in the being of All That Is, and it is a part of the heritage of all species.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第884节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "884", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0194", "zh": "可是，每个“粒子化”的单位，骑在波和粒子两者同属的意识场所设立的继续不断的冲力上。意识的每个粒子化的单位，在其内天生包含着对所有其它这种粒子的知识——再次的，因为在其它的层面，单位是如波般运作。基本上，这些单位运动得比光还快，以你们的说法，它们慢下来以形成物质。（停顿。）再次的，这些单位可被认作为存有或力量，而它们能以任意一种方式运作。形而上的说，意识单位可被认作是一切万有采取行动以形成（你们的）世界的那一点——那永不终止的创造性灵感的即刻接触，进入精神性的焦点，那确然神圣的本源的变形，这本源从神圣事实的更大实相中，将物质世界带入了存在。再次的，科学上来说，这些单位能被认作是物质的建造材料。伦理上来说，CU’s代表世界在价值完成中的壮观的基础，因为每个意识单位都彼此相关，为另一个意识单位的一部分，每个都参与“在生灭的经验”的整个完形中。我们将看看这如何应用于你们对物种的态度，以及人与其它有意识的存有和与它们共有的行星之间的关系。", "en": "(Pause at 9:04, one of many.) Each “particleized” unit, however, rides the continual thrust set up by fields of consciousness, in which wave and particle both belong. Each particleized unit of consciousness contains within it inherently the knowledge of all other such particles—for at other levels, again, the units are operating as waves. Basically the units move faster than light,2 slowing down, in your terms, to form matter. (Pause.) These units can be considered, again, as entities or as forces, and they can operate as either. Metaphysically, they can be thought of as the point at which All That Is acts to form [your] world—the immediate contact of a never-ending creative inspiration, coming into mental focus, the metamorphosis of certainly divine origin that brings the physical world into existence from the greater reality of divine fact. Scientifically, again, the units can be thought of as building blocks of matter. Ethically, the CU’s represent the spectacular foundations of the world in value fulfillment, for each unit of consciousness is related to each other, a part of the other, each participating in the entire gestalt of mortal experience. And we will see how this applies to your attitudes toward specieshood, and man’s relationship with other conscious entities and the planet he shares with them.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第889节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "889", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0200", "zh": "鲁柏对他读到的文章感到激愤，而他义愤填膺的说，这种做法在生物上是不道德的。我通常避免用“道德”或“不道德”这种字眼，因为定义因人而异。可是，那做法的确涉及了生物上的侵犯，一个违背大自然的流动及意图的做法。在其中，一种生命形式被迫违背自己的价值完成，而就因为这种涉及了其他种生命的态度，才使得犹太人在二战时集中营的恐怖成为可能。", "en": "Ruburt was incensed by the article that he read, and he said indignantly that such procedures involve a biological immorality. I usually avoid terms like “morality” or “immorality,” since their definitions vary according to the individual. The proceedings, however, do involve a biological violation, a going against nature’s flow and intent, a process in which a form of life is made to go against its own value fulfillment, and it is because of such attitudes involving other kinds of life that the horrors of the Jewish war camps were made possible.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第910节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "910", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0150", "zh": "它们是这游戏的规则，在你们的系统之内，违背它们便是自蹈疯狂。没有它们，系统本身看来会像是疯癫的，唯有它们赋予系统任何神智。就价值完成而言，历经多世转世，心灵所经历的成长之惊人，不下于胎儿长成成人时身体的成长。", "en": "They are the rules of the game, and within your system you cannot go against them without courting madness. The system itself would appear insane without them, and only they impart any sanity. In terms of value fulfillment over a period of reincarnations, there is as startling a psychic growth as there is physical growth from a fetus into an adult.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第446节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "446", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0124", "zh": "你通常只对一个系统有觉知，而且一般只会意识到你自己除了是那个系统的一个生物以外，什么都不是。我这里指的是目前的人类。这些心理结构经由价值完成不断扩增它们的能力，形成新的实相并且在它们之内行动。不应该忘记的是，这些环境系统是由它们之内的居民创造的，而这包含你们自己的系统在内。", "en": "You are as a rule aware of one system only and not generally conscious of yourself as anything but a creature of that system. I refer here to humanity at this time. These psychological structures through value fulfillment, ever enlarge their abilities to form new realities and to act within them. It should not be forgotten that these environmental systems are directly created by those who dwell within them, and this includes your own.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第306节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "306", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0122", "zh": "不要太认真看待小神的连结，因为这不是一个贴切的字眼，但它带出我想要描绘的概念，只不过有点扭曲了。它们的价值完成比你的价值完成深入相当多：它们的经验更加充实，它们的知识层次也比较高。", "en": "Take the minor god connection lightly as the term is a poor one but brings out the idea I want to portray, though it is somewhat distorted. Their value fulfillment is considerably deeper than yours: their experience fuller and their knowledge at a higher level.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第305节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "305", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0100", "zh": "这里我还要再多谈一下鲁柏的全我所具备的那些特质，正是那些特质让我可以和你们的场域沟通。不过，这里我只希望指出，你们自己的自我和潜意识之间的沟通，必须靠你们自己，而自我和个人潜意识之间的沟通愈容易，整体当下人格的力量、能力、潜力和价值完成就愈大。", "en": "I am going to say more here concerning those characteristics of Ruburts whole self, which allow me to communicate with your field. Here, however, I merely wished to make the point that this communication between your own egos and your own subconscious must depend upon yourselves, and the easier the communication between the ego and the personal subconscious the greater the strength, abilities, potentialities and value fulfillment of the present personality as a whole.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第152节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "152", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B08", "title": "新手怎么用：把困难当冒险，追随快乐", "note": "新手怎么用？把困难当成挑战、当成你为自己选的创造性冒险的一部分——你选它，正因为它最适合你个人的价值完成；在为自己调和许多观念与矛盾时，你也在为许多人领路。享受自然本身就有一种价值完成，能把你从许多束缚里释放出来；知性不必孤军奋战，它受自己其他部分支持。灵魂会剥除一切象征，在一种价值完成里完美它自己。一个“层面”就是为了存有而形成、以便顺着不同层次进行价值完成的模式。而创造往往就是价值完成的结果——所有可能性都必然会浮现，但每一次浮现，在最真实的意义上都是一次创造。所以与其苦撑，不如把工作想成一场令人兴奋的冒险。", "src": "第4、151、62、428、571、51、16、50节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 4 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 151 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 62 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 428 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 571 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 51 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 16 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 50 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-056-e0234", "zh": "然而，现在已是时候了，你们该视这种困难为挑战，是你们自己选择的一个创造性冒险的一部分。你们选择了那冒险，因为它是最适合你们自己个人的价值完成的那一种。在为你们自己调解许多观念和矛盾时，你们也替许多别人领路。再次的，如果你们将你们的工作认作是一场冒险，一场令人兴奋的创造性冒险，而不是以你们老说法的「工作」的话，会有相当大的帮助！", "en": "It is time that you regarded such difficulties instead as challenges that are a part of a creative adventure that you have yourselves chosen. You chose the adventure because it was the kind best suited to your own individual value fulfillment. In reconciling the many concepts and contradictions for yourselves, you also lead the way for many others. It would, again, help considerably if you thought of your work more as an adventure, an exciting creative adventure, than of work in your old terms.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第4节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "4", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0099", "zh": "约瑟，我相信我应该再一次建议你，每天短暂散步一会儿，这样的建议也许看起来微不足道，但其实不然，而且事实会证明非常有益。在享受自然之时，的确有一种价值完成，可以让你从许多束缚中得到解脱。", "en": "I believe I should once again suggest, Joseph, a daily short walk for you. Such suggestions may appear trivial, yet they are not, and will prove most beneficial. There is indeed a value fulfillment within the enjoyment of nature that can release you from many restraints.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0046", "zh": "还有，基于某些我暂且不说的理由，在你们的物质宇宙之内的心灵模式，就像你们知道的，并没有被无限期地维持。据我所知，没有任何种类的完形一直保持不变。但心灵完形以价值完成的方式发展，而且在一个物质模式首次出现时，就已经知道这个逐渐建立的完形将会被维持多久。", "en": "Also, for reasons that I will for now withhold, the psychic patterns within your physical universe are not maintained, as you know, indefinitely. As far as I know, no gestalt of any kind remains the same. But psychic gestalts develop in terms of value fulfillment, and it is known at the first appearance of a physical pattern how long the particular to-be-built-up gestalt will be maintained.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第62节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "62", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0141", "zh": "于是他们进而了解他们基本的合一，同时仍保有自己的本体，因为变化从不止息。加引号地说：“等到”这份体认到来时，内在的价值完成早已创造了新的实相。我能为你们贴近地近似出来的答案是这样：目的就是存在。这与你们那种（加下划线）蛮力求存的想法不同。", "en": "They come to understand then their basic oneness, while still retaining their own identity, since change is never still. In quotes: “By the time” this realization comes, inner value fulfillment has already created new realities. The answer, as closely as I can approximate it for you, is this: the purpose is being. This is something different than your idea (underlined) of brute survival.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第428节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "428", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0154", "zh": "在如此做时，灵魂继续创造出新的、可被探索的内在实相。而当灵魂向可谓相反的方向工作时，它自己剥除了所有的象征、所有的代表，而以不同的方式用它的意识学着探索它自己直接的经验。在它与经验之间没有夹着象征，它在一种价值完成中完美它自己，那是你目前所无法了解的，除了象征性地了解外。", "en": "In so doing, the soul continually creates new varieties of inner reality to be explored. Working in the opposite direction, so to speak, the soul divests itself of all symbols, all representations, and using its consciousness in a different way learns to probe its own direct experience. Without symbols to come between it and experience, it perfects itself in a kind of value fulfillment that you presently cannot understand except symbolically.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第571节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "571", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0018", "zh": "之所以有耐久性，是因为有就价值完成而言的持续扩展。你们的伪装物质宇宙的确，出于必要，诱使你们以为时间存在于过去、现在和未来之中。只因为被建构成物质实相的意念或能量，因此才能在物质特性之下运作。", "en": "The durability is achieved because of constant expansion in terms of value fulfillment. Your camouflage physical universe does, necessarily, lead you to suppose that time exists in terms of past, present and future, simply because the idea or energy constructed into physical reality therefore operates under physical properties.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第51节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "51", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0001", "zh": "层面和层面可以也的确相互渗透，但两个层面之中的居民却浑然不知。我想要摆脱一个层面是一个地方的概念。在某些情况下它可能是一个地方，但并不都是这样。一个层面可能是一段时间。一个层面，不管你相信与否，可能只是仿佛独自存在的一丁点生命力。一个层面是为了一段时间和一个理由，表面上与其余宇宙分开的某个东西。一个层面可能停止存在。一个层面可能从空无中冒出。一个层面是为了存有而形成，以便顺着不同层次进行价值完成的模式。一个层面是有助于独特且特定的能力和成就发展的一种气候。一个层面是元素的隔离，在那里每一种元素都拥有最可能的运作空间。", "en": "Planes can and do intermix without the knowledge of the particular inhabitants of either plane. I want to get away from the idea of a plane being a place. It may be in some cases but it is not always. A plane may be a time. A plane, believe it or not, may be only one iota of vitality that seems to exist by itself. A plane is something apparently divided from the rest of the universe for a time and for a reason. A plane may cease to be. A plane may spring up where there was none. A plane is formed for entities as patterns for fulfillment along various levels. A plane is a climate conducive to the development of unique and particular capacities and achievements. A plane is an isolation of elements where each element is given the most possible space in which to function.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第16节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "16", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-056-e0010", "zh": "这个创造不只牵涉到能量单位和场域的戏法，从一个形式变换到另一个，也牵涉到新能量场的建立。这往往是价值完成的结果，在这种情况下，所有的可能性都必然会浮现，但每一个浮现的可能性就最真实的意义而言都是一个创造。", "en": "This creation involves not merely the juggling of energy units and fields, from one form to another, but also involves the setting up of new fields. This is oftentimes the result of value fulfillment, in which case all the given possibilities are bound to emerge, but each emergence is in the truest sense a creation.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第50节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "50", "only_en": false}]}]}], "reading": [], "books": [{"name": "早期课第3册", "count": 10}, {"name": "梦、进化与价值完成", "count": 10}, {"name": "早期课第2册", "count": 9}, {"name": "早期课第9册", "count": 8}, {"name": "个人与群体事件的本质", "count": 7}, {"name": "早期课第4册", "count": 7}, {"name": "早期课第7册", "count": 5}, {"name": "早期课第8册", "count": 5}, {"name": "未知的实相卷二", "count": 2}, {"name": "神奇之道", "count": 2}, {"name": "个人实相的本质", "count": 1}, {"name": "心灵的本质", "count": 1}, {"name": "早期课第6册", "count": 1}, {"name": "灵魂永生", "count": 1}, {"name": "早期课第1册", "count": 1}], "span": [1963, 1980], "stats": {"blocks": 8, "quotes": 70, "reading": 0, "reading_tagged": 0, "tagged": 0, "only_en": 5}};
